    "description": "Net Trade Advantage is a zero-sum metric. For each trade, advantage_for_team_a = team_a_value_now - team_b_value_now. Team A receives that value; Team B receives its negative. Each manager's net_advantage is the sum of their per-trade advantages across every trade they participated in. Because the metric is zero-sum, the sum across all managers equals 0. A positive net_advantage means a manager extracted more present-day asset value from trades than they gave up; a negative value means the opposite. wins counts trades where the manager's side is currently worth more; win_rate is wins / trades."
